body:json {
  {}
}
docs {
  Completes one pending social picture import for the authenticated, non-anonymous current user.
  Empty body (or input_avatar_path: null) records a failed/skipped attempt and returns false.
  To attach a processed image, supply {"input_avatar_path":"<current-user-uuid>/avatar-<generated-name>.jpg"}.
  The object must exist in private user-avatars Storage and be owned by the current user. Foreign/malformed/missing object paths raise 22023 (HTTP 400).
  HTTP 200 true means attached. False means no pending import, expiry after five minutes, an existing avatar, a profile edited since initialisation, or an omitted path.
  Repeated completion returns false. The normal editable avatar RPC remains separate and can replace/remove the imported picture.
  Anonymous/unauthenticated requests are rejected (42501; HTTP 403 for an authenticated anonymous session, 401 without authentication).
  A confirmed false result lets the application remove its unused upload. An uncertain network result must not delete a potentially attached image.
}
